# The smolvm release this crate builds against, and the one the runner image
# installs. The crate is only half of what the runner needs: the same release
# supplies the agent rootfs and the ext4 disk templates the library reaches for
# at runtime, and a guest agent from one version talking to a library from
# another is not a combination anybody tests. So this file is the one place the
# version is named — .mise/fetch-smolvm clones the source at tag= and refuses a
# tree that is not commit=, then applies smolvm.patch, and the image build installs the release tarball of
# the same tag, refusing one whose digest is not the sha256- line for its
# architecture (the release's own checksums.sha256).
# libkrun-commit= is the libkrun the release's lib/libkrun.so was built from
# (smolvm's libkrun submodule at commit=). The image build rebuilds it from that
# commit with libkrun.patch applied, and refuses a build whose exported krun_*
# symbols differ from the release's.
tag=v1.32.1
commit=6221ee6ac0d54cb9d810f5d34768c64433635bb8
libkrun-commit=6d17e58286fd3af79fcdfd358ac094b32e6acf18
libkrunfw-commit=8ba5fe2219b5c407ce1824d1c2dcf39adff84d8e
libkrunfw-kernel-sha256=f410638061a165c12f42ab871d2f3fcd525515359b5faeee80969cff84524df9
sha256-linux-x86_64=6d6ddac20e11c1a09409df99232b9a559866a554b413d8d0fd82976d7669108b
sha256-linux-arm64=2c7147cc8e13ffe9446c915517ccdc7a812d9421e4f6133fdebadc6bd2214800
